<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:
minor-latin">Hi <span style="background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">&lt;Name&gt;</span><o:p></o:p></span></p>]]></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" height="300" >
<td tEditID="c1r2" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r2" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal">The American Red Cross relies on our dedicated partners
like you to fulfill our mission of helping patients battling sickle cell
disease receive the most compatible blood.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal" align="center" style="margin-bottom:0in;text-align:center;
line-height:normal"><b><i>One in three African American blood donors are a match for people
with sickle cell disease.</i></b><o:p></o:p></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The
success of your previous blood drives enables us to help these patients
tremendously. During the summer months when blood donations tend to drop,
sickle cell patients are still relying on blood donors to donate blood.</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal"><o:p></o:p></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">June offers
a special time of recognition, with </span><b style="font-size: 12pt;"><a href="https://vimeo.com/696167273/ac3155272a">Dr. Charles R. Drew’s<span style="mso-bidi-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;
font-weight:normal"></span></a><a class="msocomanchor" id="_anchor_1" href="https://americanredcross.sharepoint.com/teams/SponsorMarketingTeam/Shared%20Documents/General/Segments/Diversity/African%20American/Diversity%20Calendar/Charles%20Drew%20Bday-World%20Sickle%20Cell%20Day-Juneteenth/2024/Diversity%20Calendar%20-%20Outlook%20Email%20Templates%20-%20June%202024.docx#_msocom_1" language="JavaScript" name="_msoanchor_1">[FR1]</a>&nbsp;</b><b style="font-size: 12pt;">
birthday<a></a></b><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> on June
3 and </span><b style="font-size: 12pt;">World Sickle Cell Awareness Day</b><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> and </span><b style="font-size: 12pt;">Juneteenth</b><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> on June 19.
It’s the perfect time to highlight Black communities coming together — and what
better way to celebrate community than by hosting a blood drive to support
those in the community battling ailments such as sickle cell disease?</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal"><o:p></o:p></p>

<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal">Please
consider hosting a Red Cross blood drive this summer. Let’s find time to talk.
Would &lt;<span style="background:yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">Day of Week</span>&gt;
of this week work, or would next week be better?<o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Sincerely,</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal">







</p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal"><span style="mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;background:
yellow;mso-highlight:yellow">&lt;AM/SAM/ABM Name&gt;</span><o:p></o:p></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal"><o:p></o:p></p>

